<p><code>manifest.json</code> holds the full hashes and the counts, signed by the log's key <code>did:key:z6Mkw1CVxsPj9utYp7VXWEbuuGM9Ev47itwKu1UfKd5ByxR9</code>
(type <code>histor.dataset/v1</code>, Ed25519 over RFC 8785 JSON). It also carries the signed tree head the
export started under (tree size 1,867,699), so any label id below can be checked
against the live log with <code>GET https://histor.modelmarket.dev/api/v1/labels/&lt;id&gt;/proof</code>.</p>
<h2 class="relative group flex items-baseline">
	<a id="fields" class="block pr-1.5 text-lg md:absolute md:p-1.5 md:opacity-0 md:group-hover:opacity-100 md:right-full" href="#fields" rel="nofollow">
		<span class="header-link"><svg class="text-gray-500 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-gray-200 w-4" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden="true" role="img" width="1em" height="1em" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" viewBox="0 0 256 256"><path d="M167.594 88.393a8.001 8.001 0 0 1 0 11.314l-67.882 67.882a8 8 0 1 1-11.314-11.315l67.882-67.881a8.003 8.003 0 0 1 11.314 0zm-28.287 84.86l-28.284 28.284a40 40 0 0 1-56.567-56.567l28.284-28.284a8 8 0 0 0-11.315-11.315l-28.284 28.284a56 56 0 0 0 79.196 79.197l28.285-28.285a8 8 0 1 0-11.315-11.314zM212.852 43.14a56.002 56.002 0 0 0-79.196 0l-28.284 28.284a8 8 0 1 0 11.314 11.314l28.284-28.284a40 40 0 0 1 56.568 56.567l-28.285 28.285a8 8 0 0 0 11.315 11.314l28.284-28.284a56.065 56.065 0 0 0 0-79.196z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span>
	</a>
	<span>
		Fields
	</span>
</h2>
<p>Fields whose shape varies between servers are JSON text (<code>*Json</code>), so every file loads as a flat
table. Digests are SRI strings (<code>sha256-…</code>) over the RFC 8785 form of the value.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>servers</strong> — <code>id</code> (stable per name+endpoint), <code>name</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>endpoint</code>
(<code>https://…</code> or <code>npm:</code>/<code>pypi:</code> for packages), <code>transport</code>, <code>registry</code>, <code>version</code>, <code>repository</code>,
<code>firstListed</code>/<code>lastListed</code>, <code>delisted</code>, <code>skipReason</code> (why it was not dialled), <code>lastStatus</code> and
<code>lastDetail</code> (the last attempt's outcome), <code>lastObserved</code>, <code>toolCount</code>, <code>toolSetDigest</code> (join to
toolsets), <code>firstPinned</code>, <code>unchangedSince</code>, <code>attempts</code>, <code>observations</code>, <code>changes</code>,
<code>blockMatches</code>/<code>adviseMatches</code>/<code>recordMatches</code>, <code>classifierFlags</code>, <code>chainLabel</code> (latest label id), <code>page</code>.</li>
<li><strong>toolsets</strong> — <code>digest</code>, <code>toolsJson</code>: per tool the four members the digest covers, as served
(<code>name</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>inputSchema</code>, and <code>outputSchema</code> when sent).</li>
<li><strong>tool_extras</strong> — <code>digest</code>, <code>extrasJson</code>: <code>{"tools": {name: {member: value}}}</code>, every member a tool
carried beyond those four (<code>annotations</code>, <code>_meta</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>icons</code>, <code>execution</code>, vendor fields),
only for tools that carried one. Join from <code>servers.toolExtrasDigest</code>: <code>""</code> there means observed with
none, null not observed since HISTOR keeps them (2026-10-22). Not part of the MTL/1 digest or of any
label; its digest is SHA-256 over sorted-key JSON, not RFC 8785 (prices in <code>_meta</code> are fractions).</li>
<li><strong>extras_changes</strong> — <code>serverId</code>, <code>observedAt</code>, <code>fromExtrasDigest</code> → <code>toExtrasDigest</code>, <code>summaryJson</code>:
per tool, every annotation that moved (<code>[before, after]</code>) and every other member added, removed or
changed; <code>escalations</code> names tools that stopped saying <code>readOnlyHint: true</code> or started saying
<code>destructiveHint: true</code>.</li>
<li><strong>changes</strong> — <code>serverId</code>, <code>observedAt</code>, <code>fromToolSetDigest</code> → <code>toToolSetDigest</code>, <code>summaryJson</code>
(tools added, removed and changed, with the field that moved), <code>labelId</code> (the signed continuity label).
For a package, <code>fromPackageVersion</code> → <code>toPackageVersion</code>: the last version that served the old list
and the one that served the new list (null for remote servers and before 2026-10-26).
For every change, <code>fromServerVersion</code> → <code>toServerVersion</code>: the version the server reported about itself
(<code>serverInfo</code>) in the last run that served the old list and in the run that saw the new one; and
<code>fromRegistryVersion</code> → <code>toRegistryVersion</code>: the version the MCP registry listed for the entry at those
two runs. A change whose versions are equal on both sides moved at an unchanged version: a record keyed
on the version cannot see it. Server versions come from every run since the log began (null when the
server reported none); registry versions are recorded since 2026-10-28 and null before, and null for
entries that come from no registry.</li>
<li><strong>scans</strong> — <code>toolSetDigest</code>, <code>patternSet</code>, <code>matchesJson</code> (rule code, tier, severity, tool, where).
The rules are in <code>pattern-set.json</code>. A match is a pattern hit to look at, not a verdict.</li>
<li><strong>classifications</strong> — <code>toolSetDigest</code>, <code>model</code>, <code>verdictJson</code>: an LLM's advisory reading of the
tool set. Not reproducible, so it never enters the signed log.</li>
<li><strong>package_observations</strong> — every run of an npm/PyPI package, failed ones included, oldest first:
<code>serverId</code>, <code>observedAt</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>packageVersion</code> (the version the sandbox ran), <code>toolSetDigest</code>
(join to toolsets; null when the run failed), <code>subjectDigest</code>, <code>toolExtrasDigest</code>, <code>toolCount</code>, and
<code>serverName</code>/<code>serverVersion</code> as the server reported them in legacy initialization or modern result
metadata (often not the package version), <code>registryVersion</code> (what the MCP registry listed for the entry
at that run; since 2026-10-28), and <code>protocolVersion</code> when recorded (otherwise null).
<code>packageVersion</code> is recorded since 2026-10-26; older rows have it null. <code>launchJson</code>
says how the run was launched: <code>observer</code> (the sandbox's version), <code>image</code>/<code>imageTag</code>/<code>runtime</code>/
<code>entry</code>, <code>network</code> (<code>no route out</code>: a server that fetches something at startup gets nothing), and
<code>supplied</code> when HISTOR started it again with configuration: the env variable NAMES it set to
placeholders (never a value), start <code>args</code>, <code>pins</code>. The same version can serve different tools under
other launch args or with the network, so compare lists launched alike. Null on runs before it was
recorded (2026-10-26). Remote servers are not in this file: their record is their changes.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="relative group flex items-baseline">
	<a id="how-a-change-is-counted" class="block pr-1.5 text-lg md:absolute md:p-1.5 md:opacity-0 md:group-hover:opacity-100 md:right-full" href="#how-a-change-is-counted" rel="nofollow">
		<span class="header-link"><svg class="text-gray-500 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-gray-200 w-4" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden="true" role="img" width="1em" height="1em" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" viewBox="0 0 256 256"><path d="M167.594 88.393a8.001 8.001 0 0 1 0 11.314l-67.882 67.882a8 8 0 1 1-11.314-11.315l67.882-67.881a8.003 8.003 0 0 1 11.314 0zm-28.287 84.86l-28.284 28.284a40 40 0 0 1-56.567-56.567l28.284-28.284a8 8 0 0 0-11.315-11.315l-28.284 28.284a56 56 0 0 0 79.196 79.197l28.285-28.285a8 8 0 1 0-11.315-11.314zM212.852 43.14a56.002 56.002 0 0 0-79.196 0l-28.284 28.284a8 8 0 1 0 11.314 11.314l28.284-28.284a40 40 0 0 1 56.568 56.567l-28.285 28.285a8 8 0 0 0 11.315 11.314l28.284-28.284a56.065 56.065 0 0 0 0-79.196z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span>
	</a>
	<span>
		How a change is counted
	</span>
</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>What is compared.</strong> Per tool, the members in <code>toolsets</code>: <code>name</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>inputSchema</code>, and
<code>outputSchema</code> when the server sent one. Tools are sorted by name and the set is hashed in its RFC 8785
form, so tool order, object key order and JSON whitespace never make a change. Strings are compared as
sent (a description that only gains a space is a change), and so is the order of arrays inside a schema
(<code>required</code>, <code>enum</code>). Other members (<code>title</code>, <code>annotations</code>, <code>_meta</code>, <code>icons</code>) are not in the digest;
they are kept in <code>tool_extras</code>, and their changes in <code>extras_changes</code>.</li>
<li><strong>When.</strong> A change is a successful read whose digest differs from the server's previous successful
read. Remote polling cadence depends on the observer configuration and available capacity; packages are read
once per published version. States between polls can be missed. Every recorded change is
recorded, including one that goes back to a list the server showed before.</li>
<li><strong>Failed reads.</strong> A timeout, an HTTP error, a server that asks for credentials or one HISTOR does not
dial is never a change: the server keeps its last list, and <code>lastStatus</code> says how the last attempt
went. A server that never answered without credentials has no tool set.</li>
<li><strong>One client.</strong> HISTOR reads without credentials, from one host. Lists that differ by user, account or
region are not seen; a list that differs per session shows up as changes alternating between two digests.</li>
<li><strong>What moved.</strong> In <code>summaryJson</code>, a modified tool names the members that moved: <code>description</code> as a
word diff, <code>inputSchema</code>/<code>outputSchema</code> as JSON paths (a parameter description is a path ending in
<code>"description"</code>). A renamed tool is a removal plus an addition. <code>detail</code> is <code>names-only</code> when one side
could not be digested; that change compares names only.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="relative group flex items-baseline">
	<a id="load-it" class="block pr-1.5 text-lg md:absolute md:p-1.5 md:opacity-0 md:group-hover:opacity-100 md:right-full" href="#load-it" rel="nofollow">
		<span class="header-link"><svg class="text-gray-500 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-gray-200 w-4" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden="true" role="img" width="1em" height="1em" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" viewBox="0 0 256 256"><path d="M167.594 88.393a8.001 8.001 0 0 1 0 11.314l-67.882 67.882a8 8 0 1 1-11.314-11.315l67.882-67.881a8.003 8.003 0 0 1 11.314 0zm-28.287 84.86l-28.284 28.284a40 40 0 0 1-56.567-56.567l28.284-28.284a8 8 0 0 0-11.315-11.315l-28.284 28.284a56 56 0 0 0 79.196 79.197l28.285-28.285a8 8 0 1 0-11.315-11.314zM212.852 43.14a56.002 56.002 0 0 0-79.196 0l-28.284 28.284a8 8 0 1 0 11.314 11.314l28.284-28.284a40 40 0 0 1 56.568 56.567l-28.285 28.285a8 8 0 0 0 11.315 11.314l28.284-28.284a56.065 56.065 0 0 0 0-79.196z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span>
	</a>
	<span>
		Load it
	</span>
</h2>
<pre><code class="language-python"><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span> pandas <span class="hljs-keyword">as</span> pd
servers = pd.read_json(<span class="hljs-string">"servers.jsonl.gz"</span>, lines=<span class="hljs-literal">True</span>)
changes = pd.read_json(<span class="hljs-string">"changes.jsonl.gz"</span>, lines=<span class="hljs-literal">True</span>)
</code></pre>
<pre><code class="language-sql"><span class="hljs-comment">-- DuckDB</span>
<span class="hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> name, <span class="hljs-built_in">count</span>(<span class="hljs-operator">*</span>) <span class="hljs-keyword">AS</span> changes <span class="hljs-keyword">FROM</span> <span class="hljs-string">'changes.jsonl.gz'</span> c
<span class="hljs-keyword">JOIN</span> <span class="hljs-string">'servers.jsonl.gz'</span> s <span class="hljs-keyword">ON</span> s.id <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> c.serverId <span class="hljs-keyword">GROUP</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">BY</span> name <span class="hljs-keyword">ORDER</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">BY</span> changes <span class="hljs-keyword">DESC</span> LIMIT <span class="hljs-number">20</span>;

<span class="hljs-comment">-- Changes in which nothing moved but tool descriptions</span>
<span class="hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">count</span>(<span class="hljs-operator">*</span>) <span class="hljs-keyword">FROM</span> (<span class="hljs-keyword">SELECT</span> summaryJson::JSON <span class="hljs-keyword">AS</span> s <span class="hljs-keyword">FROM</span> <span class="hljs-string">'changes.jsonl.gz'</span>)
<span class="hljs-keyword">WHERE</span> s<span class="hljs-operator">-</span><span class="hljs-operator">&gt;&gt;</span><span class="hljs-string">'detail'</span> <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> <span class="hljs-string">'full'</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">AND</span> json_array_length(s<span class="hljs-operator">-</span><span class="hljs-operator">&gt;</span><span class="hljs-string">'added'</span>) <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> <span class="hljs-number">0</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">AND</span> json_array_length(s<span class="hljs-operator">-</span><span class="hljs-operator">&gt;</span><span class="hljs-string">'removed'</span>) <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> <span class="hljs-number">0</span>
  <span class="hljs-keyword">AND</span> json_array_length(s<span class="hljs-operator">-</span><span class="hljs-operator">&gt;</span><span class="hljs-string">'modified'</span>) <span class="hljs-operator">&gt;</span> <span class="hljs-number">0</span>
  <span class="hljs-keyword">AND</span> list_bool_and(list_transform(from_json(s<span class="hljs-operator">-</span><span class="hljs-operator">&gt;</span><span class="hljs-string">'modified'</span>, <span class="hljs-string">'["JSON"]'</span>), m <span class="hljs-operator">-</span><span class="hljs-operator">&gt;</span> json_keys(m<span class="hljs-operator">-</span><span class="hljs-operator">&gt;</span><span class="hljs-string">'fields'</span>) <span class="hljs-operator">=</span> [<span class="hljs-string">'description'</span>]));
</code></pre>
<p><code>scripts/change_kinds.py</code> in the code repository sorts every change by the fields it touched.</p>
<h2 class="relative group flex items-baseline">
	<a id="what-it-is-not" class="block pr-1.5 text-lg md:absolute md:p-1.5 md:opacity-0 md:group-hover:opacity-100 md:right-full" href="#what-it-is-not" rel="nofollow">
		<span class="header-link"><svg class="text-gray-500 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-gray-200 w-4" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden="true" role="img" width="1em" height="1em" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" viewBox="0 0 256 256"><path d="M167.594 88.393a8.001 8.001 0 0 1 0 11.314l-67.882 67.882a8 8 0 1 1-11.314-11.315l67.882-67.881a8.003 8.003 0 0 1 11.314 0zm-28.287 84.86l-28.284 28.284a40 40 0 0 1-56.567-56.567l28.284-28.284a8 8 0 0 0-11.315-11.315l-28.284 28.284a56 56 0 0 0 79.196 79.197l28.285-28.285a8 8 0 1 0-11.315-11.314zM212.852 43.14a56.002 56.002 0 0 0-79.196 0l-28.284 28.284a8 8 0 1 0 11.314 11.314l28.284-28.284a40 40 0 0 1 56.568 56.567l-28.285 28.285a8 8 0 0 0 11.315 11.314l28.284-28.284a56.065 56.065 0 0 0 0-79.196z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span>
	</a>
	<span>
		What it is not
	</span>
</h2>
<ul>
<li>A tool list is what a server advertised to an anonymous client on that day. Servers that need
credentials, or that refused HISTOR, have no tool set here (<code>lastStatus</code>, <code>skipReason</code> say why).</li>
<li>Pattern matches and classifier flags point at text worth reading; they do not say a server is malicious.</li>
<li>A change is a change in the definitions, not a judgement of it. Most are ordinary releases.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="relative group flex items-baseline">
	<a id="cite" class="block pr-1.5 text-lg md:absolute md:p-1.5 md:opacity-0 md:group-hover:opacity-100 md:right-full" href="#cite" rel="nofollow">
		<span class="header-link"><svg class="text-gray-500 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-gray-200 w-4" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden="true" role="img" width="1em" height="1em" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" viewBox="0 0 256 256"><path d="M167.594 88.393a8.001 8.001 0 0 1 0 11.314l-67.882 67.882a8 8 0 1 1-11.314-11.315l67.882-67.881a8.003 8.003 0 0 1 11.314 0zm-28.287 84.86l-28.284 28.284a40 40 0 0 1-56.567-56.567l28.284-28.284a8 8 0 0 0-11.315-11.315l-28.284 28.284a56 56 0 0 0 79.196 79.197l28.285-28.285a8 8 0 1 0-11.315-11.314zM212.852 43.14a56.002 56.002 0 0 0-79.196 0l-28.284 28.284a8 8 0 1 0 11.314 11.314l28.284-28.284a40 40 0 0 1 56.568 56.567l-28.285 28.285a8 8 0 0 0 11.315 11.314l28.284-28.284a56.065 56.065 0 0 0 0-79.196z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span>
	</a>
	<span>
		Cite
	</span>
</h2>
<p>Artamokhov, A. (2026). <em>HISTOR snapshot 2026-11-09: MCP tool definitions and how they change</em> [Data set].
Zenodo. <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23512759" rel="nofollow">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23512759</a></p>
<p>This is the DOI of every snapshot, and it opens the newest one, where the same query gives other numbers. Once this snapshot is archived, its own version DOI is listed at <a href="https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/" rel="nofollow">https://histor.modelmarket.dev/datasets/</a>; cite that one next to any number: <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23512759" rel="nofollow">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23512759</a>.
Also on Hugging Face: <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/alexar76/histor-mcp-tool-definitions" rel="nofollow">https://huggingface.co/datasets/alexar76/histor-mcp-tool-definitions</a> (tag <code>snapshot-2026-11-09</code>).</p>
<h2 class="relative group flex items-baseline">
	<a id="license-and-rights" class="block pr-1.5 text-lg md:absolute md:p-1.5 md:opacity-0 md:group-hover:opacity-100 md:right-full" href="#license-and-rights" rel="nofollow">
		<span class="header-link"><svg class="text-gray-500 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-gray-200 w-4" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden="true" role="img" width="1em" height="1em" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" viewBox="0 0 256 256"><path d="M167.594 88.393a8.001 8.001 0 0 1 0 11.314l-67.882 67.882a8 8 0 1 1-11.314-11.315l67.882-67.881a8.003 8.003 0 0 1 11.314 0zm-28.287 84.86l-28.284 28.284a40 40 0 0 1-56.567-56.567l28.284-28.284a8 8 0 0 0-11.315-11.315l-28.284 28.284a56 56 0 0 0 79.196 79.197l28.285-28.285a8 8 0 1 0-11.315-11.314zM212.852 43.14a56.002 56.002 0 0 0-79.196 0l-28.284 28.284a8 8 0 1 0 11.314 11.314l28.284-28.284a40 40 0 0 1 56.568 56.567l-28.285 28.285a8 8 0 0 0 11.315 11.314l28.284-28.284a56.065 56.065 0 0 0 0-79.196z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span>
	</a>
	<span>
		License and rights
	</span>
</h2>
<p>The compilation, digests, labels, scans and verdicts are CC-BY-4.0. Tool names, descriptions and schemas are reproduced as each server
published them; their rights stay with their authors. They are included so the definitions can be
studied and checked. A server operator who wants out: open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/alexar76/histor" rel="nofollow">https://github.com/alexar76/histor</a> with the
endpoint or host. Opted-out servers are left out of every later snapshot.</p>
